---
title: Schools Reinventing Counties
---
{% extends "layouts/base.njk" %}

{% block head %}
<style>
  /* ── OVERVIEW ───────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .overview-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 80px; align-items: start; margin-top: 48px; }
  .overview-cards-col { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }

  /* ── THREE PILLARS ON CREAM ─────────────────────────────────── */
  .pillars-cream { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 16px; margin-top: 3.5rem; }

  /* ── THE WORLD BUILD ────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .world-header { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 80px; align-items: start; margin-bottom: 3.5rem; }
  .world-header-body { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--civic); }
  .world-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 2fr 3fr; gap: 80px; align-items: center; }
  .world-placeholder {
    aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
    background: rgba(22,43,77,0.5);
    border: 1.5px solid rgba(22,43,77,0.8);
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  }
  .world-placeholder-lbl {
    font-family: 'Pixelify Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em; color: rgba(139,163,194,0.55); text-align: center;
    text-transform: uppercase; line-height: 1.8;
  }
  .world-lbl {
    font-family: 'Pixelify Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 14px;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgba(139,163,194,0.5); margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .world-lbl + .card-list { margin-bottom: 36px; }
  .world-card-list li { color: var(--civic); }
  .world-card-list li::before { background: var(--red); }

  /* ── QUOTE BAND ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .quote-band { border-top: 4px solid var(--red); background: var(--cream); padding: 80px 80px; }
  .quote-inner { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 28% 1fr; gap: 56px; align-items: center; }
  .quote-mark-wrap { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; justify-content: flex-end; }
  .quote-mark-wrap img { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; opacity: 0.12; }
  .quote-text {
    font-family: 'Big Shoulders Display', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 700; font-size: clamp(24px, 2.8vw, 40px);
    color: var(--ink); line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.01em; margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
  .quote-attr { font-size: 14px; color: var(--gray); line-height: 1.6; }
  .quote-attr strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }

  /* ── WHY IT WORKS ───────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .stakes-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 80px; align-items: start; margin-top: 48px; }
  .stakes-cards { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 40px; }

  /* ── RESPONSIVE ──────────────────────────────────────────── */
  @media (max-width: 1024px) {
    .overview-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 48px; }
    .pillars-cream { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
    .world-header { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 32px; }
    .world-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 48px; }
    .stakes-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 48px; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .quote-band { padding: 64px 20px; }
    .quote-inner { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 24px; }
    .quote-mark-wrap img { max-width: 72px; opacity: 0.08; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .pillars-cream { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}

<!-- HERO -->
<div class="page-hero">
  <div class="page-hero-content">
    <div class="page-hero-eyebrow">The Program</div>
    <h1 class="page-hero-h1">Schools Reinventing Counties.</h1>
    <p class="page-hero-sub">
      A statewide community design program built in Minecraft Education. Students explore their county, investigate a real local challenge, design a solution, and pitch it to the leaders who can act on it.
    </p>
    <div class="page-hero-cta">
      <a href="/submit/" class="btn-cream">Get Your School Involved</a>
      <a href="#" class="btn-ghost-civic">Download the Field Guide →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="page-hero-visual">
    <img src="/assets/kids-collage.png" alt="Students collaborating on a civic design project">
  </div>
</div>

<!-- OVERVIEW -->
<section class="sec sec-cream">
  <h2 class="sec-h2 sec-h2-dark page-h2 h2-block">The program that turns<br>civics into action.</h2>
  <div class="overview-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="sec-body">Schools Reinventing Counties connects classroom learning to authentic community challenges. Students don't just learn about local government — they investigate a real problem, build a solution, and pitch it to the people in charge.</p>
      <p class="sec-body">The program is built on one principle: a real location, a specific problem, and a real audience produce deeper student work than an open-ended prompt. When students know their ideas can reach the people actually making decisions, they stop playing and start advocating.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="overview-cards-col">
      <div class="info-card">
        <div class="info-card-lbl">The World</div>
        <p class="info-card-text">A Minecraft world built around your students' actual county — not a generic environment</p>
      </div>
      <div class="info-card">
        <div class="info-card-lbl">The Challenge</div>
        <p class="info-card-text">A real community challenge, not a fictional scenario</p>
      </div>
      <div class="info-card">
        <div class="info-card-lbl">The Pitch</div>
        <p class="info-card-text">A live pitch to local leaders who are present to listen — not just to evaluate</p>
      </div>
      <div class="info-card">
        <div class="info-card-lbl">Standards</div>
        <p class="info-card-text">Standards-aligned across multiple subject areas</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- DESIGN PROCESS -->
<section class="sec sec-navy">
  <h2 class="sec-h2 sec-h2-light page-h2 h2-body">Eight steps.<br>One community.</h2>
  <p class="sec-intro sec-intro-light sec-intro-mb">
    Every team follows the same design process. Understanding comes before designing.
  </p>
  <div class="grid-4">
    <div class="pillar pillar-sm">
      <div class="pillar-num">01</div>
      <h3 class="pillar-title">Explore</h3>
      <p class="pillar-body">Observe the community before attempting to improve it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pillar pillar-sm">
      <div class="pillar-num">02</div>
      <h3 class="pillar-title">Listen</h3>
      <p class="pillar-body">Meet guides, local leaders, historians, and subject matter experts.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pillar pillar-sm">
      <div class="pillar-num">03</div>
      <h3 class="pillar-title">Investigate</h3>
      <p class="pillar-body">Ask questions to understand how history, geography, and culture shape the place.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pillar pillar-sm">
      <div class="pillar-num">04</div>
      <h3 class="pillar-title">Understand</h3>
      <p class="pillar-body">Connect what you've learned and identify the problems worth solving.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pillar pillar-sm">
      <div class="pillar-num">05</div>
      <h3 class="pillar-title">Imagine</h3>
      <p class="pillar-body">Brainstorm possibilities before committing to a direction.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pillar pillar-sm">
      <div class="pillar-num">06</div>
      <h3 class="pillar-title">Design</h3>
      <p class="pillar-body">Create a solution grounded in what the community actually needs.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pillar pillar-sm">
      <div class="pillar-num">07</div>
      <h3 class="pillar-title">Build</h3>
      <p class="pillar-body">Bring the idea to life in Minecraft — every block should have a purpose.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pillar pillar-sm">
      <div class="pillar-num">08</div>
      <h3 class="pillar-title">Share</h3>
      <p class="pillar-body">Record a 3-minute walkthrough and enter the Battle of the Counties.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- THREE PILLARS (expanded on cream) -->
<section class="sec sec-cream">
  <h2 class="sec-h2 sec-h2-dark page-h2 h2-body">Three pillars.<br>One program.</h2>
  <p class="sec-intro sec-intro-wide sec-intro-mb">
    Built at the intersection of three disciplines that rarely share a classroom — and produce something no single subject can on its own.
  </p>
  <div class="pillars-cream">
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-eyebrow card-eyebrow-red">Pillar 01</div>
      <h3 class="card-title">STEM & Digital Literacy</h3>
      <p class="card-body">Spatial reasoning, coding logic, and engineering design in a native digital environment. Students think like engineers while building real community solutions.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-eyebrow card-eyebrow-red">Pillar 02</div>
      <h3 class="card-title">Civic Engagement</h3>
      <p class="card-body">Systems thinking, community problem-solving, and public policy exploration through authentic local challenges and real decision-makers.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-eyebrow card-eyebrow-red">Pillar 03</div>
      <h3 class="card-title">Academic Esports</h3>
      <p class="card-body">Real-time collaboration, consensus-building, and high-stakes presentation — in a competitive format that students actually want to win.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- THE WORLD BUILD -->
<section class="sec sec-navy">
  <div class="world-header">
    <h2 class="sec-h2 sec-h2-light page-h2">Built for your county.</h2>
    <p class="world-header-body">Every participating county gets a custom Minecraft Education world grounded in real local geography, landmarks, and community life. Your staff builds nothing — the world comes ready to explore.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="world-grid">
    <div>
      <div class="world-placeholder">
        <div class="world-placeholder-lbl">Image placeholder<br>Minecraft county world</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="world-lbl">What's inside every world</div>
      <ul class="card-list world-card-list" style="margin-bottom: 36px;">
        <li>A Community Hub where students begin and select their challenge area</li>
        <li>County-specific landmarks, neighborhoods, and civic spaces</li>
        <li>NPCs representing real community voices: leaders, historians, scientists, and experts</li>
        <li>A Community Design Mentor who presents the Design Challenge</li>
        <li>A designated build zone for student solutions</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="world-lbl">How the world is made</div>
      <ul class="card-list world-card-list">
        <li>Built by Lifeboat Studios — no work required from school staff</li>
        <li>Grounded in real county geography, history, and community priorities</li>
        <li>Runs on Minecraft Education via school or district licensing</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- QUOTE -->
<div class="quote-band">
  <div class="quote-inner">
    <div class="quote-mark-wrap">
      <img src="/assets/quote-mark.svg" alt="">
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="quote-text">"This is not about playing a game. It is about student voice, civic engagement, and showing our students that their ideas can lead real change."</p>
      <div class="quote-attr"><strong>Dr. Stefan Bean</strong>, Orange County Superintendent of Schools</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- WHY IT WORKS -->
<section class="sec sec-cream" style="padding-top: 80px;">
  <h2 class="sec-h2 sec-h2-dark page-h2 h2-block">Why this model works.</h2>
  <div class="stakes-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="sec-body">A real location, a specific problem, and a real audience produce deeper student work than an open-ended prompt. That's the core insight the program is built on.</p>
      <p class="sec-body">Students who know their ideas can reach the people actually making decisions don't treat the work as schoolwork. They treat it as a platform. The build gets more detailed. The research gets more thorough. The pitch gets rehearsed.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="stakes-cards">
        <div class="info-card">
          <div class="info-card-lbl">Place</div>
          <p class="info-card-text">Their county, their community, their neighbors — not a fictional scenario</p>
        </div>
        <div class="info-card">
          <div class="info-card-lbl">Problem</div>
          <p class="info-card-text">Housing, transportation, sustainability, public space — real challenges with no easy answer</p>
        </div>
        <div class="info-card">
          <div class="info-card-lbl">Audience</div>
          <p class="info-card-text">Local leaders who are present to listen, not just to evaluate</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <a href="/#competition" class="btn-primary">See the Battle of the Counties →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- CTA BAND -->
<div class="cta-band">
  <div class="cta-band-inner">
    <h2 class="cta-band-h2">Ready to bring this<br>to your students?</h2>
    <p class="cta-band-body">
      Schools in participating counties can register now. The worlds come built, training is provided, and the competition is structured. You bring the students.
    </p>
    <div class="cta-band-btns">
      <a href="/educators/" class="btn-white">For Educators</a>
      <a href="/submit/" class="btn-white">Submit a Project</a>
      <a href="/partners/" class="btn-ghost-white">Partner with us →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% endblock %}
